# GSAP animation

- Store a reference to every tween or timeline that outlives a single frame. You cannot kill what you did not keep.
- Kill each of them on `destroy()`, on resize, and on any state change that invalidates the animation. Never leave orphaned tweens running against a destroyed object.
- Before starting a tween on properties that may already be animating, kill the previous tween on that target first.
- If an animation is cancelled mid-flight, restore the properties it mutated (`revert()` or an explicit reset) so the object is not left half-animated.
- `PixiPlugin` is registered once in `src/index.ts`. Do not register it again elsewhere.

```typescript
// ✅
private hoverTween: gsap.core.Tween | null = null;

public override destroy(options?: DestroyOptions): void {
	this.hoverTween?.kill();
	this.hoverTween = null;
	super.destroy(options);
}
```
